# Required packages — install-pkg.sh hard-fails if any of these can't be
# installed, because a later step in the same run depends on them
# unconditionally: git (the zinit and TPM bootstrap clones in
# install-restore.sh) and zsh (the chsh default-shell step in
# install-services.sh).
#
# Keep this list as small as it can honestly be. A hard-fail turns a wrong
# or renamed package name into no install at all rather than a degraded one,
# and CLAUDE.md rule 8 means these names are checked against
# packages.fedoraproject.org by hand — never against a live dnf. Anything
# that merely breaks a *feature* belongs in desktop.lst, which says so
# loudly and carries on.
#
# The suckless build toolchain (gcc, make, patch, pkgconf-pkg-config) moved
# to packages/build.lst, which install-suckless.sh installs itself right
# before it builds.
#
# Format: one package name per line. '#' starts a comment (whole-line or
# trailing). Blank lines ignored.

git
zsh
